+### 4.3 conversation_list
+
+Requests a page of the authenticated user's conversation summaries ([conversation-list](../hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "conversation_list",
+  "limit": 20,
+  "before": {
+    "updatedAt": "2026-09-30T10:00:00.000Z",
+    "sessionId": "0f1e2d3c-4b5a-4968-8776-655443322110"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type                                       | Required | Description                                                                                 |
+| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string                                     | Yes      | `"conversation_list"`                                                                       |
+| `limit`  | number                                     | No       | Maximum summaries to return (non-negative integer; defaults to 50 and caps at 200 in store) |
+| `before` | `{ updatedAt: string; sessionId: string }` | No       | Cursor naming the last summary already seen                                                 |
+
+Semantics:
+
+- The user is always the connection's own `session.userId`; any `userId` field on the frame is ignored ([validated by: delivers the authenticated user conversation_list newest-first, supports limit and before paging, and answers an empty array when the user has none](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L120)).
+- Like `ping`, `conversation_list` is a read and does not wait behind the per-session message lock, so a user can open the conversation switcher while a turn is streaming ([validated by: answers conversation_list immediately while a turn is streaming on the same session without waiting for the per-session lock](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L167)).
+- If `limit` is present and is not a non-negative integer, or if `before` is present without a parseable `updatedAt` string and non-empty `sessionId` string, the server answers `error` with `INVALID_MESSAGE` and no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED with no stream_end when the session store lacks listFor, SERVER_ERROR when listFor throws, and INVALID_MESSAGE when limit or before is malformed while accepting valid requests](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L211)).
 
